<x:xmpmeta xmlns:x="adobe:ns:meta/">
  <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#">
    <rdf:Description xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" rdf:about="">
      <dc:title>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">No evil plans while we are dancing</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:title>
      <dc:description>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">&lt;p&gt;Adora has a secret to keep from the Rebellion: she is in love with Catra. Since they were teenagers, actually. But when she was at the Horde with the brunette, she had to suppress those feelings because she was taught that it was a weakness and something a good soldier won't do. Present time, she knows those feelings are valid and worthwhile, but she knows nothing about how to love. So, she reads an extensive guide about "how to properly love women". &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;She finds the answer to her question: how to love? However, she wasn't expecting love to be made of complicated poses, delighted facial expressions and dirty talking. And zero clothes.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Adora feels hot and bothered after that, and the fact that Catra is at Princess Prom teasing her doesn't help at all...&lt;/p&gt;</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:description>
      <dc:creator>
